#. STRINGS.CODEX.A1_CLONEDRABBITS.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A1_CLONEDRABBITS.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"<smallcaps>[Voice Recognition Initialized]\n"
"[Subject Identified: B111]</smallcaps>\n"
"\n"
"[LOG BEGINS]\n"
"\n"
"[A throat clears.]\n"
"\n"
"B111: We are now reliably printing healthy, living subjects, though all have exhibited unusual qualities as a result of the cloning process.\n"
"\n"
"[Chattering sounds can be heard.]\n"
"\n"
"B111: Odd communications, abnormal excrescenses, and vestigial limbs have been seen in all subjects thus far, to varying degrees of severity. It seems that bypassing or accelerating juvenility halts certain critical stages of development. Brain function, however, appears typical.\n"
"\n"
"[Chattering.]\n"
"\n"
"B111: T-They also seem quite happy.\n"
"\n"
"B111: Dr. Broussard, signing off.\n"
"\n"
"[LOG ENDS]"
msgstr ""
"<smallcaps>[音声認識初期化]\n"
"[対象認識: B111]</smallcaps>\n"
"\n"
"[ログ開始]\n"
"\n"
"(咳払い)\n"
"\n"
"B111: 我々はついに健康的で生存している被検体を確実に製造することができるようになったが、複製プロセスの結果すべてが異常な品質を指している。\n"
"\n"
"(鳴き声)\n"
"\n"
"B111: これまでのところ、全ての被検体で奇妙なコミュニケーション、異常突起、四肢の退化が様々な程度で見られた。若年期を迂回または加速させると特定の重要な発達段階が停止するようだ。しかし、脳機能は典型的な模様。\n"
"\n"
"(鳴き声)\n"
"\n"
"B111: 被検体はとても幸せそうに見える。\n"
"\n"
"B111: ブルサード博士より、通信終わり。\n"
"\n"
"[ログ終了]"

