#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"<b>Praise for <i>Swept Into the Stars</i>:</b>\n"
"\n"
"\"Unspeakably beautiful.\"\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—Li Fu, author of <i>The Moments Between Now and Tomorrow</i></indent>\n"
"\n"
"\"Stunning compositions by one of the world's most celebrated scientific minds.\"\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—Quinn Kelly, The Ballyhoo Book Review</indent>\n"
"\n"
"\"I dare you to read this and not feel inspired.\"\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—Dolores Greene, Newplane Publishing House</indent>\n"
"\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<b>『星々に誘われて』への賞賛：</b>\n"
"\n"
"「言葉では言い表せないほど美しい。」\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—リ・フゥ (『The Moments Between Now and Tomorrow』の著者)</indent>\n"
"\n"
"「世界で最も著名な科学者の一人による、息を呑むような作品。」\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—クウィン・ケリー (The Ballyhoo Book Review)</indent>\n"
"\n"
"「これを読んで、インスピレーションを受けない人がいるだろうか。」\n"
"\n"
"<indent=10%>—ドローレス・グリーニー (Newplane Publishing House)</indent>\n"
"\n"
"------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "<b>FOREWORD</b>"
msgstr "<b>まえがき</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC4_FOREWORD.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid ""
"\"Our advancements as a species do not occur in a vacuum. Our success is built on the efforts of those who came before us. Their explorations, ideas, hopes, and breakthroughs illuminate ours, and give us a reason to keep pushing forward. Science is our vehicle, but people—friends, strangers, and rivals alike—are our purpose.\"\n"
"\n"
"That's the short version of the monologue that Dr. Austin Higby delivered at least once a week.\n"
"\n"
"Dr. Higby was a staunch advocate of collaboration. His research took astrobiology into exciting new territory, a feat he attributed to the contributions of co-authors and sources from every branch of science. He also had a deep appreciation for the arts. Many of his colleagues attended their first theater production at his invitation, myself included.\n"
"\n"
"During one of his rotations at the Gravitas Facility, I asked him how he found time for it all. He laughed. \"It finds <i>me!</i>\"\n"
"\n"
"Three months later, he and the crew of the Starsweep II vanished while on a now-infamous mission for the Clear Skies Coalition. No trace of their spacecraft has ever been found.\n"
"\n"
"Then these writings were discovered among Dr. Higby's personal files. Dozens upon dozens of poems and essays so profound that they make the reader feel transported to another place and time...one that feels at once familiar and completely alien.\n"
"\n"
"<i>Swept Into the Stars</i> is a labour of love by countless friends, colleagues, students, and fans who worked tirelessly to organize and edit Dr. Higby's words.\n"
"\n"
"With permission from the Higby family, this edition also includes the farewell speech he had penned for the retirement announcement he never had a chance to make.\n"
"\n"
"Higby would be equal parts proud and embarrassed.\n"
"\n"
"I miss you, my friend. I hope we meet again someday, so you can tell me what wonders found you out there at the edges of the universe.\n"
"\n"
"This one's for you. For all of us.\n"
"\n"
"Always,\n"
"<indent=10%>Emily G.</indent>\n"
"\n"
"<i>One hundred percent of the proceeds from Dr. Austin Higby's estate, including the sale of this book, will be donated to the Higby Memorial Scholarship fund for students who wish to pursue combined studies in science and the arts.</i>"
msgstr ""
"「人類としての進歩は、真空の中で起こるものではありません。私たちの成功は、先人たちの努力の上に築かれています。彼らの探求、アイデア、希望、そして画期的な発見は、私たちの成功を照らし出し、前進し続けるための理由を与えてくれます。科学は私たちの乗り物ですが、友人、見知らぬ人、ライバルなど、人々こそが私たちの目的なのです。」\n"
"\n"
"これは、オースティン・ヒグビー博士が少なくとも週に一度語っていた独白の要約です。\n"
"\n"
"ヒグビー博士は共同研究の熱心な支持者でした。彼の研究は宇宙生物学を刺激的な新しい領域へと導きました。彼は、その功績をあらゆる科学分野の共著者や情報源の貢献のおかげだと考えていました。彼はまた、芸術への深い理解も持っていました。彼の同僚の多くは、彼の招待で初めて演劇を鑑賞しました。私もその一人です。\n"
"\n"
"グラビタス研究所での研修中、私は彼にどうやってそれら全てに時間を割いているのか尋ねました。彼は笑いました。 「向こうが私を見つけるんだよ！」\n"
"\n"
"三か月後、彼とスタースイープII号の乗組員は、クリアスカイズ連合の悪名高いミッションの最中に姿を消しました。彼らの宇宙船の痕跡は未だ見つかっていません。\n"
"\n"
"そして、ヒグビー博士の個人ファイルの中から、これらの文章が発見されました。何十もの詩やエッセイは、読者を別の場所と時間へと運んでしまうほど深く、まるで馴染み深くも、全く異質な世界へと誘います。\n"
"\n"
"『星々に誘われて』は、数え切れないほどの友人、同僚、学生、そしてファンが、ヒグビー博士の言葉を整理し編集するために精力的に取り組んだ、愛情のこもった作品です。\n"
"\n"
"ヒグビー家の許可を得て、この版には、彼が発表する機会を得られなかった退職発表のために書き下ろした送別スピーチも収録されています。\n"
"\n"
"ヒグビーはきっと誇りに思うと同時に、恥ずかしくも思うでしょう。\n"
"\n"
"友よ、君がいなくて寂しいよ。いつかまたお会いできることを願っています。宇宙の果てで、どんな不思議な体験をしたのか、教えてください。\n"
"\n"
"これはあなたに。私たちみんなに。\n"
"\n"
"いつまでも\n"
"<indent=10%>エミリー・G.</indent>\n"
"\n"
"<i>本書の売上を含む、オースティン・ヒグビー博士の遺産の収益はすべて、科学と芸術の融合研究を志す学生のためのヒグビー記念奨学金基金に寄付されます。</i>"

