#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Starnacles share DNA with both arthropods and echinoderms, though they retain elements of the latter's fascinating digestive mechanism.\n"
"\n"
"During feeding, a Starnacle's stomach is pushed out through its small mouthpiece to envelop the nutrient source. Digestion is completed outside the body, and the stomach then retracts.\n"
"\n"
"The process can be disturbing to witness. Fortunately, the organism's mouthpiece is located on its underside."
msgstr ""
"ホシツボは節足動物と棘皮動物の両方とDNAを共有していますが、棘皮動物の興味深い消化機構の要素も受け継いでいます。\n"
"\n"
"摂食時、ホシツボは胃を小さな口器から押し出し、栄養源を包み込みます。消化は体外で完了し、その後胃は体内に戻ります。\n"
"\n"
"この過程は見ていて不快に感じるかもしれませんが、幸いなことに、口器は体の下面にあります。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Organism"
msgstr "水棲生物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLANKTONCORAL.TITLE"
msgid "Starnacle"
msgstr "ホシツボ"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Plug Slugs are fuzzy gastropoda that are able to cling to walls and ceilings thanks to an extreme triboelectric effect caused by friction between their fur and various surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"This same phenomenon allows the Plug Slug to generate a significant amount of static electricity that can be converted into power.\n"
"\n"
"The increased amount of static electricity a Plug Slug can generate when domesticated is due to the internal vibration, or contented 'humming', they demonstrate when all their needs are met."
msgstr ""
"びりびりナメクジは毛むくじゃらの腹足類です。壁や天井に張り付くことができますが、それは体毛と各種表面との摩擦で起こる極端な摩擦帯電のおかげです。\n"
"\n"
"これと同様の原理で、びりびりナメクジが発生させた大量の静電気を電力に変換することができます。\n"
"\n"
"びりびりナメクジは飼い慣らされると静電気の量が増加しますが、これは体内の振動、つまり満足を示す「ハミング」によるものです。これは全ての生理的欲求が満たされたときに見せる習性です。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "飼い慣らせる動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PLUGSLUG.TITLE"
msgid "Plug Slug"
msgstr "びりびりナメクジ"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Pokeshells are bottom-feeding invertebrates that consume the waste and discarded food left behind by other creatures."
msgstr "ポークシェルは他の生物の食べ残しやゴミを消費する底生の無脊椎動物です。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "They have formidably sized claws that fold safely into their shells for protection when not in use."
msgstr "未使用時には自身の殻を守るための折りたためる手ごろな大きさの爪を持っています。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "As Pokeshells mature they must periodically shed portions of their exoskeletons to make room for new growth."
msgstr "ポークシェルが成長するにつれ、成長の余地を作るだけの外骨格を脱ぎ変えなければなりません。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER4
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.BODY.CONTAINER4"
msgid "Although the most dramatic sheds occur early in a Pokeshell's adolescence, they will continue growing and shedding throughout their adult lives, until the day they eventually die."
msgstr "最も劇的な脱ぎ変えはポークシェルの成体初期に訪れますが、その後は死亡するまで外骨格は成長し続けます。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Pokeshells"
msgstr "ポークシェル属"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "飼い慣らせる動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.POKESHELL.TITLE
