#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"\"Kelpole\" is the colloquial name given to <i>Osculateus venerandum</i>, a small free-moving organism spawned from microscopic eggs that attach themselves to <link=\"SEATREE\">Tower Kelp</link>.\n"
"\n"
"These unusual critters possess only a few hundred neurons and rely primarily on leaf mimicry to camouflage them from predators during their brief lives.\n"
"\n"
"Formerly considered flora, Kelpoles were eventually reclassified as fauna due to their frequent inclusion on marine biologists' lists of top ten most adorable creatures. The term \"flona\" was rejected out of hand."
msgstr ""
"「ケルポール」とは、<i>Osculateus venerandum</i>という、<link=\"SEATREE\">タワーケルプ</link>に付着した微小な卵から孵化した、小さな自由遊泳生物の通称です。\n"
"\n"
"この珍しい生物は、わずか数百個の神経細胞しか持たず、短い一生の間、捕食者から身を守るために主に葉に擬態しています。\n"
"\n"
"かつては植物と考えられていたケルポールは、海洋生物学者が選ぶ「最も愛らしい生き物トップ10」に頻繁に登場することから、最終的に動物に分類変更されました。「flona」という用語は即座に却下されました。"

